Send the carrier's roaming protocol, and read the files stock reads at boot

Two gaps, both from diffing the whole AP->CP stream against the capture with
nothing filtered out.

**SET_DATA_PROFILE carried the wrong roaming protocol.** frame+0x76 was a copy
of the home protocol; stock sends the carrier's own:

    ch0xf5 services.telus.com   pdp 2   stock roaming 3   ours 2
    ch0xf5 sos                  pdp 2   stock roaming 3   ours 2
    ch0xf5 ims                  pdp 2   stock roaming 2   ours 2   (agree)

`ims.db` has carried the column all along -- its rows say roaming 3 for both of
those APNs next to protocol 2 -- and MMSitApn already parsed it into
`->roaming`. Nothing passed it on. The field feeds the profile table the CP
matches URSP route selection against, which is the machinery behind the
2253/168 refusals, so a wrong value there is not cosmetic. Needs
exynos-modem >= r26 for samsung_sit_build_set_data_profile_roaming.

**The elementary-file pass, the largest single divergence in the capture.**
Stock issues 121 SIM_IO exchanges on ch 0xf5 and 167 on 0xf6 before its IMS
context; we issued 27 and 25. Most of the volume is two files -- EF_OPL
(0x6fc6) and EF_PNN (0x6fc5), read record by record 50 and 20-49 times -- and
the rest is one GET_RESPONSE plus one read across the standard set. 37 files in
stock's own order, ch 0xf5's sequence first then the ones only 0xf6 touches.
mm_sit_client_read_ef() already does a whole file read including the record
loops, so this is the list and the order; a card without a file answers with a
status word and it is skipped, so one list serves both stacks. Nothing is kept.

This was previously written off as "cosmetic operator-name lookups". It was
also excluded from the sequence-alignment score, which is how a filtered 69%
was reported where the real figure was 36%. Measuring the unfiltered stream is
the only honest way to run this diff.

The boot-config fake peer gains the 37 exchanges, each refused with 6a82 as a
card lacking the file would, so read_ef() gives up after one frame and the
frame count there is the file count.

What is NOT fixed here, because it is not a code path: `sp.telus.com` goes out
with roaming 3 where stock sends 1, and the apn-type masks differ --
`xcap` 1024 vs stock's 2048, `mobile.bm` 7 vs 23. Those are the values in our
generated `ims.db`: it is built from the Mist_OS carriersettings rather than the
device's vendor ones, and XCAP lands at bit 10 because that proto enum has no
MCX. Fixing them means regenerating the database from the device's own carrier
settings, not editing the plugin.

